==== hyperbricks yaml {!{quote_feed}} ====
quote_feed:
  - type: api_render
  - endpoint: https://example.com/api/quotes
  - method: POST
  - headers:
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
  - body: |
      {"topic":"$topic","limit":"$limit"}
  - querykeys:
      - topic
      - limit
  - queryparams:
      topic: focus
      limit: "3"
  - jwtsecret: local-secret
  - jwtclaims:
      aud: fixture
  - inline: |
      {{ range .Data }}<p>{{ .quote }}</p>{{ end }}
  - values:
      fallback:
        - title: Empty state
          body: No quotes were returned.
        - title: Error state
          body: The upstream request failed.
==== explainer ====
API_RENDER keeps request fields, query allow-lists, JWT settings, inline template content, and array-of-map values as data.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@type": "<API_RENDER>",
  "body": "{\"topic\":\"$topic\",\"limit\":\"$limit\"}\n",
  "endpoint": "https://example.com/api/quotes",
  "headers": {
    "Accept": "application/json",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  },
  "inline": "{{ range .Data }}<p>{{ .quote }}</p>{{ end }}\n",
  "jwtclaims": {
    "aud": "fixture"
  },
  "jwtsecret": "local-secret",
  "method": "POST",
  "querykeys": [
    "topic",
    "limit"
  ],
  "queryparams": {
    "limit": "3",
    "topic": "focus"
  },
  "values": {
    "fallback": [
      {
        "body": "No quotes were returned.",
        "title": "Empty state"
      },
      {
        "body": "The upstream request failed.",
        "title": "Error state"
      }
    ]
  }
}
